{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"polonium-unvagrant-larva","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# The live-DC readiness gate (`serverInfo` 200) is too weak for the contract 3fe5 asserts, so a timing flake would be misattributed to an image degrade\n\n## The gap\n\nBoth live-DC workflows gate on the same signal — poll `/rest/api/2/serverInfo` until 200:\n\n* `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml:526-536`\n* `.github/workflows/jira-dc-epic-link-probe.yml:50-60`\n\nBut `tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py::_assert_project_capabilities` then asserts the instance\nexposes the **Jira Software (GreenHopper) custom fields** `Epic Link` and `Epic Name`\n(`_REQUIRED_FIELDS`). **`serverInfo` answering 200 does not imply those fields are registered.**\n\n## Proof, measured on the probe workflow\n\nRun 30944211742 shares the harness's readiness gate and queries the field inventory immediately after\nit passes:\n\n```\nWait for Jira DC to become ready : 19:39:01 -> 19:47:33   (8m32s, serverInfo polling)\nRun the Epic-Link clear probe    : 19:47:33 -> 19:47:34   (1 second later)\n\nfield 'Epic Link' absent from an inventory of 27 field(s); names present:\n  ['Archived','Archiver','Attachment','Comment','Created','Creator','Images','Key','Last Viewed',\n   'Log Work','Original Estimate','Progress','Project','Remaining Estimate','Resolved','Status',\n   'Sub-Tasks','Time Spent','Time Tracking','Updated','Votes','Watchers','Work Ratio',\n   'Σ Original Estimate','Σ Progress','Σ Remaining Estimate','Σ Time Spent']\n```\n\n27 fields, **every one a system field, zero `customfield_*`**. The read was authorised and well-formed;\nthe plugin had simply not registered its fields one second after `serverInfo` went green.\n\n## Why the harness has not failed on this — and why that is luck, not safety\n\nThe harness is not more careful than the probe; it is just **slower afterwards**. It installs\ndependencies and then runs a ~41-minute suite, so by the time the first test's fixture reaches\n`_assert_project_capabilities`, minutes have elapsed and GreenHopper is up. The probe asks in the first\nsecond and sees the real state.\n\nSo the harness's margin is incidental. If a run reached that fixture faster (dependency cache warm,\nfewer collected tests, a reordering) or the plugin initialised slower, `_assert_project_capabilities`\nwould raise **`PROVISIONING FAILED: this instance exposes no ['Epic Link', 'Epic Name'] field(s)`** and\nits own message would tell the reader to *\"Re-run the capability map against the current image and\nupdate `_REQUIRED_FIELDS` if the instance genuinely renamed them\"* — i.e. it would be diagnosed as the\n**3fe5 image degrade** when the true cause is timing. A misattributing flake, and an expensive one:\nit points the next reader at the image and the declared contract instead of at readiness.\n\nThis is the same family as 3fe5 itself. 3fe5's lesson was that an unverifiable contract must not pass\nvacuously; this is the mirror — a contract asserted **too early** fails loudly for the wrong reason.\n\n## Fix\n\nGate on the CAPABILITY, not a proxy. After `serverInfo` goes green, poll `/rest/api/2/field` until every\nname in `_REQUIRED_FIELDS` is present, under its own bounded budget, and fail with the inventory dump\nwhen it never arrives. `serverInfo` is the wrong predicate for anything depending on a plugin's fields.\n\nBest placed in the readiness helper both tiers share (`conftest.wait_for_jira_dc_ready`) so the workflow\nstep and the fixture cannot diverge, with the workflow-level curl loop kept as the cheap first gate.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] readiness for the live-DC tiers requires every `_REQUIRED_FIELDS` name to be present in\n      `/rest/api/2/field`, not merely a 200 from `serverInfo`\n- [ ] the wait has its own bounded budget, and on expiry fails with the observed field inventory in the\n      message so the failure is self-diagnosing\n- [ ] `_assert_project_capabilities`'s message no longer attributes a missing Epic field to an image\n      degrade without first distinguishing \"not registered yet\" from \"not offered by this image\"\n- [ ] the probe workflow and the harness workflow share one readiness definition, so they cannot drift\n- [ ] a test pins that a field-inventory response containing only system fields is treated as NOT ready\n      rather than as a degraded image\n\n## Testing\n\n    pytest tests/unit/test_live_jira_dc_provisioning.py tests/unit/test_live_jira_dc_conftest.py -q\n    make lint && make typecheck\n\nThe load-bearing assertion is the negative one: a system-only inventory must read as \"not ready\".\nWithout it this stays a latent flake that only appears when a run happens to be fast.","id":"9790-cafa-dffa-462e","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Live-DC readiness (serverInfo 200) is too weak for 3fe5's declared field contract; a timing flake would be misattributed to an image degrade"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785873039363742001,"uuid":"e34be42e-e6ba-4dab-aa75-ba766a7cd141"}